<h2>Segment 275 &mdash; an opponent invokes Dharmakirti</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s275S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w1">kha cig</span>, <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s275q1">de ltar</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w2">&#x27;dod pa</span> de <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w3">mi &#x27;thad par</span> thal, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w4">dpal ldan</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w5">chos kyi grags pa</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w6">lung</span> dang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w7">&#x27;gal ba</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s275p1">phyir</span>, <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s275q2">der thal</span>, de&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w8">gzhung</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s275p2">las</span>, <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s275q3">gal te</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w9">de</span> <span class="u case" data-d="6" data-l="s275p3">yang</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s275q4">mthong med</span> la, , <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s275q5">brten nas</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w10">gzugs</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w11">gzhan</span> &#x27;byung &#x27;gyur na, , zhes <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w12">dgra</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w13">gnyen</span> gnyis <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s275p4">kyis</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w14">skyes bu</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w15">gcig</span> gi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w16">gzugs</span> la <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w17">bltas pa</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s275q6">de&#x27;i tshe na</span>, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w18">skyes bu</span> de&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w19">gzugs</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w20">mdzes</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w21">mi mdzes</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w22">gnyis</span> su gnas kyang , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w23">gzugs</span> de dang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w24">dgra</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w25">gnyen</span> gnyis kyi <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s275q7">bar du</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w26">las</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w27">gzugs</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w28">skyes</span> pas, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w29">dgra</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w30">gnyen</span> gnyis po des gzugs <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w31">mdzes</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w32">mi mdzes</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w33">gnyis ka</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s275p5">ma</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w34">mthong ba</span>, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w35">grangs can</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s275p6">gyis</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w36">khas blangs pa</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w37">de</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w38">&#x27;gog byed</span> kyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w39">rigs pa</span> kha spos pas <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s275q8">khyod kyi de la gnod pa</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s275p7">phyir</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w40">zer</span> na</span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s275S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w1">One</span> comes and makes the following <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w40">claim</span>: Your <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w2">position</span>, <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s275q1">as just explained</span>, is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w3">mistaken</span>, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s275p1">for</span> it <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w7">goes against</span> a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w6">statement</span> of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w4">glorious</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w5">Dharmakirti</span>. <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s275q2">This is quite surely the case</span>, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s275p7">for</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s275p2">in</span> his major <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w8">work</span> [entitled The Commentary on Valid Perception] he says, <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s275q3">Suppose</span> you say that they <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s275q4">don&#x27;t see</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w9">it</span>, And <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s275q5">circumstances</span> cause <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w11">another</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w10">form</span>. What he&#x27;s talking about here is a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w36">belief</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s275p6">of</span> the [non- Buddhist] <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w35">Numerist School</span>. They give the case of a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w15">single</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w14">person</span> whose <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w16">physical form</span> is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w17">looked upon</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s275q6">at the same time</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s275p4">by</span> his <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w12">enemy</span>, and also by his <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w13">friend</span>. In reality, the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w18">person</span>&#x27;s <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w19">physical form</span> is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w22">both</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w20">attractive</span> and <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w21">ugly</span> at the same time. Something happens where yet another <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w27">physical form</span>, one from <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w26">karma</span>, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w28">grows up</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s275q7">between</span> the person&#x27;s true <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w23">physical form</span> and the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w24">enemy</span> and <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w25">friend</span> looking at it. Because of this <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s275p5">neither</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w29">enemy</span> nor the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w30">friend</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w34">sees</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w33">both</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w31">attractiveness</span> and the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w32">ugliness</span> together. Master Dharmakirti uses <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w39">logic</span> to <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w38">refute</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s275w37">this</span> concept, and this same logic can be used <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s275q8">against the position you have taken</span>, to prove that you are wrong.<span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s275p3"><span class="nul">Additive/concessive emphasis in this quoted hypothesis has no separate English even/also; the next And coordinates the following predicate.</span></span></span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex, Tibetan-first original with its own source preparation disclosed; no current English-first proposal read. The first Dharmakirti alone owns the sole Tibetan name. All four prose physical-form mentions, all three enemy/friend pairs and the two quality pairs retain their actual roles despite reordered English. Whole mi 'thad par, mthong med and mi mdzes retain their negatives; later ma owns neither in the distributed neither/nor construction. The quotation's dependency frame is tentatively retained as a phrase corresponding to circumstances; cause recasts the complete dependency/arising relation and is not falsely assigned to a single verb. The quoted yang has no separate exponent. Intermediate-form causality is expressed by Because of this, and the final quality clause has no separate form noun; these distributed contributions are omitted, not declared absent. Both phyir owners are distinguished by premise scope. The transferred-logic kha spos is distributed across same logic and can be used: the auto-aligned ugliness together master dharmakirti entry is retained as evidence but is not a license to steal those words. Work excludes the supplied title/major; Numerist School excludes the original bracketed non- Buddhist apparatus, whose spacing is kept verbatim. Independent reconciliation and semantic review must test these proposals; no source or binding glossary is changed.</div>
